#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# neville_theta_d

#% text
# `neville_theta_d(z, m)` gives the Neville theta function `theta_d(z | m)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `theta_d(z | m)` is `theta_3(pi*z/(2*K(m)), q)/theta_3(0, q)`, with the nome `q` of `m` (DLMF 20.1, 22.2). It is even and `theta_d(0 | m)` is 1.

#% item
# `jacobi_dn(z, m)` is `theta_d/theta_n`.

#% item
# Machine numbers and balls give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
neville_theta_d(0.5, 0.3)
#% output
#= 0.9833041936358866

#% cell
neville_theta_d(0, 0.3)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
neville_theta_d(1.0, 0.9)
#% output
#= 0.8556016964128921

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The quotient that gives `dn`:

#% cell
neville_theta_d(0.7, 0.4)/neville_theta_n(0.7, 0.4) - jacobi_dn(0.7, 0.4)
#% output
#= -1.1102230246251565e-16

